.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-history 1  "bhtune-history " 
.SH NAME
bhtune\-history \- Inspect past tune runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-history\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect past tune runs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bhtune\-history\-list(1)
List past runs, newest first
.TP
bhtune\-history\-show(1)
Show one run\*(Aqs full detail: config, initial readings, calculated results, and any PID write\-back audit rows
.TP
bhtune\-history\-revert(1)
Undo a run\*(Aqs PID write\-back, writing its recorded pre\-write P/I/D values back to the live loop. Reverts whichever `write`\-kind write\-back that run last recorded; refuses if the run has none, if that write\-back\*(Aqs pre\-read itself failed (nothing to revert to), or if the run did not use the `opcda` backend (nothing live to revert against)
.TP
bhtune\-history\-prune(1)
Delete runs older than the configured retention policy (`history\-retention`), without waiting for the next automatic startup sweep
.TP
bhtune\-history\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
